@startuml SrvcMgr_LrnManager_SeqDiagram_Runtime

actor tester
participant Dcm
participant SrvcMgr
participant Sd
participant SdExt
participant NVRAM
participant RemoteEcu


tester -> Dcm: RID 0x0612
Dcm -> SrvcMgr: SrvcMgr_Read_RID_0x0612_Data()
SrvcMgr -> Sd: Sd_RetrieveLearningTable(&TableContent)
Sd -> SdExt: SdExt_RetrieveLearningTable(&TableContent)
note right: SD_SWSEXT_0010, SD_GM_0026, RID 0x0612

tester -> Dcm: DID 0xE0CC
Dcm -> SrvcMgr: SrvcMgr_DID_E0CC_ReadData()
SrvcMgr -> Sd: Sd_GetLearningTableState(&LearningState)
Sd -> SdExt: SdExt_GetLearningTableState(&LearningState)
note right: SD_GM_0018, SD_SWSEXT_0005

tester -> Dcm: DID 0xE0CD
Dcm -> SrvcMgr: SrvcMgr_DID_E0CD_ConditionCheckRead()
SrvcMgr -> Sd:Sd_GetLearningTableState(&LearningState)
Sd -> SdExt: SdExt_GetLearningTableState(&LearningState)
note right
If the LearningState is LEARNING_INCOMPLETE
SrvcMgr will check if the number of missing services
(client section) excedes the maximum number 
specified in SDV-6001
endnote
SrvcMgr -> Sd: Sd_RetrieveIncompleteLearningReasons(&IncompleteLrng)
Sd -> SdExt: SdExt_RetrieveIncompleteLearningReasons(&IncompleteLrng)
note right
SD_SWSEXT_0015, SD_GM_0027
If IncompleteLrng.Num_Of_Missing_Services <= 400, SrvcMgr
returns E_OK to Dcm and then ReadDataLength is triggered.
endnote

Dcm -> SrvcMgr: SrvcMgr_DID_E0CD_ReadDataLength()
SrvcMgr -> Sd: Sd_RetrieveIncompleteLearningReasons(&IncompleteLrng)
Sd -> SdExt: SdExt_RetrieveIncompleteLearningReasons(&IncompleteLrng)
note right
SD_SWSEXT_0015, SD_GM_0027, SD_GM_0015
If IncompleteLrng.Num_Of_Missing_Services <= 400, SrvcMgr
returns E_OK to Dcm together with the length of the DID data (missing services IDs
from the incomplete learning table and sd missing from ssfm - via s/r port).
endnote

Dcm -> SrvcMgr: SrvcMgr_DID_E0CD_ReadData()
SrvcMgr -> Sd: Sd_RetrieveIncompleteLearningReasons(&IncompleteLrng)
Sd -> SdExt: SdExt_RetrieveIncompleteLearningReasons(&IncompleteLrng)
note right
SD_SWSEXT_0015, SD_GM_0027, SD_GM_0015
If IncompleteLrng.Num_Of_Missing_Services <= 400, SrvcMgr
returns E_OK to Dcm together with the missing services IDs
read from the client section of the incomplete learning table 
and sd missing from ssfm - via s/r port.
endnote

tester -> Dcm: DID 0xE0CE
Dcm -> SrvcMgr: SrvcMgr_DID_E0CE_ConditionCheckRead()
SrvcMgr -> Sd:Sd_GetLearningTableState(&LearningState)
Sd -> SdExt: SdExt_GetLearningTableState(&LearningState)
note right
If the LearningState is LEARNING_INCOMPLETE
SrvcMgr will check if the number of missing services
(server section) excedes the maximum number 
specified in SDV-6001
endnote
SrvcMgr -> Sd: Sd_RetrieveIncompleteLearningReasons(&IncompleteLrng)
Sd -> SdExt: SdExt_RetrieveIncompleteLearningReasons(&IncompleteLrng)
note right
SD_SWSEXT_0015, SD_GM_0027
If IncompleteLrng.Num_Of_Missing_EventGroups <= 400, SrvcMgr
returns E_OK to Dcm and then ReadDataLength is triggered.
endnote

Dcm -> SrvcMgr: SrvcMgr_DID_E0CD_ReadDataLength()
SrvcMgr -> Sd: Sd_RetrieveIncompleteLearningReasons(&IncompleteLrng)
Sd -> SdExt: SdExt_RetrieveIncompleteLearningReasons(&IncompleteLrng)
note right
SD_SWSEXT_0015, SD_GM_0027
If IncompleteLrng.Num_Of_Missing_Services <= 400, SrvcMgr
returns E_OK to Dcm together with the length of the DID data (missing services IDs
from the incomplete learning table).
endnote

Dcm -> SrvcMgr: SrvcMgr_DID_E0CE_ReadData()
SrvcMgr -> Sd: Sd_RetrieveIncompleteLearningReasons(&IncompleteLrng)
Sd -> SdExt: SdExt_RetrieveIncompleteLearningReasons(&IncompleteLrng)
note right
SD_SWSEXT_0015, SD_GM_0027
If IncompleteLrng.Num_Of_Missing_EventGroups <= 400, SrvcMgr
returns E_OK to Dcm together with the missing event groups IDs
read from the server section of the incomplete learning table.
endnote

@enduml